Include stdlib.h for _set_fmode in ltcdecode

ltcdecode.c calls _set_fmode() on Windows but includes only fcntl.h, while
the CRT declares it in stdlib.h. GCC 14 made implicit function declarations
an error, so the test program no longer compiles and `make check` stops
before running anything. ltcencode.c already includes stdlib.h.

Upstream: not submitted yet (master still lacks the include)
Applies-to: all environments

--- a/tests/ltcdecode.c
+++ b/tests/ltcdecode.c
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@
 
 #ifdef _WIN32
 #include <fcntl.h> // for _fmode
+#include <stdlib.h> // for _set_fmode
 #endif
 
 #define BUFFER_SIZE (1024)
